=== Git in Zsh
tag::config[]

(((Zsh)))(((Shell, Zsh)))
Zsh (the default shell on modern macOS) also provides excellent Git integration.

#### Command Completion
Zsh’s tab-completion is even more powerful than Bash’s. It can show you a list of available branch names and their most recent commit message as you type.

#### The Prompt
Like Bash, Nora can customize her Zsh prompt (often using a framework like **Oh My Zsh**) to show a clear visual indicator of her repo's status.

[source,bash]
----
# Example Oh My Zsh theme showing Git status
PROMPT='%~ %{$fg[blue]%}$(git_prompt_info)%{$reset_color%}%# '
----
This might show a green checkmark if her repo is clean, or a red X if she has modified files. It’s a constant "at-a-glance" status report for her creative environment.
